@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Login com senha errada → 401
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "usuario": "admin", "senha": "errada" }

### 2. Login sem campos → 400 com as mensagens de validação
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3. Login correto → 200 com token
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "usuario": "admin", "senha": "Admin@123" }

### 4. Quem sou eu → 200 com os dados do admin
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 5. Sem token → 401
GET {{base}}/auth/me

### 6. Logout → 204
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 7. Mesmo token depois do logout → 401 (prova que o logout é real)
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}